%S A000361 1,0,2,1,1,2,5,0,10,6,3,2,19,2,10,1,5,10,89,1,170,28,7,2,71,12,170,5,
%T A000361 25,10,21,0,42,26,51,10,1251,38,682,6,301,170,5833,3,2730,120,15,2,
%U A000361 271,56,2730,19,1737,170,1325,2,682,102,227,10,307,10,42,1,21
%N A000361 Binary encodings of the successive columns of the Gosper-Lafitte triangle.
%C A000361 From _M. Jeremie Lafitte (Levitas)_, Oct 01 2026: (Start)
%C A000361 Let W(n) be the bottom-to-top binary word recording the two types of congruent medial down-triangles occurring in column n of the fractal set described in A000360, with filled and empty represented by 1 and 0, respectively. Its Hamming weight is A000360(n), its number of zeros is A284556(n+1), and its length is A002487(n+1), corresponding to Stern's diatomic sequence. a(n) is the integer encoded by W(n) with the bottom digit corresponding to 2^0.
%C A000361 The underlying fractal set has positive Lebesgue measure and is a self-replicating tile with holes, the 4-reptile following the 2-reptile of Paul Lévy.
%C A000361 At each dyadic refinement, W(2m+1) is a lift of W(m). For m>0, W(2m) is obtained by merging lifts of W(m) and W(m-1) in row order. A lift sends a digit in row d to row 2d or 2d+1, depending on whether the new column is even or odd. It either retains or exchanges 0 and 1, according to the axial or lateral orientation.
%C A000361 Let P(r)={W(0),...,W(3*2^r-1)} be the word profile at refinement level r. The resulting doubling operator sends P(r) to P(r+1), with P(r)=Take[P(r+1),3*2^r]. Thus every profile persists unchanged as the first half of the next one. (End)
%D A000361 Croft, Falconer and Guy, Unsolved Problems in Geometry, Springer-Verlag, 1991; Problem of least k such that there exists a non-simply-connected k-reptile.
%D A000361 M. Jeremie Lafitte (Levitas), Sur l'Effet Noa`h en Geometrie, rapport a l'INPI, Mars 1995.
%H A000361 M. Jeremie Lafitte (Levitas), <a href="/A000361/b000361.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..9999</a>
